# CKA Lab Exercise: Cloud-Native Ceph Storage Drills (RBD, CephFS & CephNFS)

Hands-on training scenarios for the Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) exam covering Ceph cloud-native storage:
RADOS Block Device (RBD) integration, raw block devices (`volumeMode: Block`), online volume expansion, native CephFS
shared
filesystems, and CephFS exported over NFS via NFS-Ganesha.

---

## 1. Overview & Architecture

Rook-Ceph provides cloud-native, distributed storage orchestrating three distinct storage personalities on the cluster:

```text
                               ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                               │           Rook-Ceph Storage Cluster                   │
                               └─────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘
                                                         │
                ┌────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┐
                ▼                                        ▼                                        ▼
   ┌───────────────────────────┐           ┌───────────────────────────┐           ┌───────────────────────────┐
   │         Ceph RBD          │           │       Native CephFS       │           │         Ceph NFS          │
   │      (Block Storage)      │           │    (Shared Filesystem)    │           │    (NFS-Ganesha over FS)  │
   ├───────────────────────────┤           ├───────────────────────────┤           ├───────────────────────────┤
   │ CSI: rbd.csi.ceph.com     │           │ CSI: cephfs.csi.ceph.com  │           │ CSI: nfs.csi.k8s.io       │
   │ Access: ReadWriteOnce     │           │ Access: ReadWriteMany     │           │ Access: ReadWriteMany     │
   │ Mode: Filesystem / Block  │           │ Mode: Filesystem          │           │ Mode: Filesystem          │
   │ StorageClass:             │           │ StorageClass:             │           │ StorageClass:             │
   │   {{ cka_lab_rbd_storage_class | default('rook-ceph-block') }}          │           │   {{ cka_lab_cephfs_storage_class | default('rook-cephfs') }}             │           │   {{ cka_lab_ceph_nfs_storage_class | default('ceph-nfs-csi') }}          │
   └───────────────────────────┘           └───────────────────────────┘           └───────────────────────────┘
```

### On-Demand Auxiliary Layer

Like iSCSI (`07-iscsi/`) and Fibre Channel SAN (`08-fc/`), Ceph is an **on-demand auxiliary homelab layer** `[HOMELAB
AUXILIARY]`:

- **Activation**: Deployed and managed on demand using Ansible:
  ```bash
  make preprod-ceph
  ```
- **Status Inspection**: Check daemon and cluster health:
  ```bash
  make preprod-ceph-status
  ```
- **CKA Exam Scope**: In the CKA exam, candidates encounter standard Kubernetes storage abstractions (`volumeMode:
  Block`,
  `volumeDevices`, `ReadWriteMany` access modes, `allowVolumeExpansion: true`, and PVC expansion). Ceph provides the
  real
  distributed backend in this homelab to practice these concepts with live storage.

